# REQUIRES: verilator
# (11-08: the runs pin --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct, the defaults before then, so that the
# link counts and registers checked below stay those of the feature under test.)
# Staged links as memories (`--staged-link-memories`): the staged links of one
# producer port to one reader class keep their first registers as one
# distributed-RAM memory, an entry per producer instance, written at the
# producer's passes; each link's second register loads the memory's read at
# its own copy position (distinct in the frame: one read port). Exact against
# the target, channels stalled or not, at the same host cycles as the staged
# registers (static-link-kinds.test's designs and flags), and the report:
# - the broadcast's four lane accumulators read by the top: one memory of four
#   16-bit entries in place of 64 first registers (232 -> 168 register bits);
# - the arbiter tree with zero-latency links and chains: two memories;
# - one producer port, a bit to each of four readers (staged-bits): two.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/broadcast
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bc --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --share-links --compact-links --staged-links --staged-link-memories Lane 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BC
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BCUSE < %t/bc/schedule.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BCSIM < %t/bc/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/bc/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/bc/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bc/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=H0
# RUN: %t/bc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=60 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=H60
# BC: staged: 11 links, 168 register bits; staged memories: 1 (4 links), 64 bits, 9 LUTRAM LUTs
# BC: link kinds: distributed 1 64 10; block 0 0 0.0; ultra 0 0 0; registers 11 168
# BCUSE: link use Lane Top_model 16 4 4 distributed 0
# BCSIM: %Lane_acc_staged_mem0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <4 x 16
# H0: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles in 1200 host cycles
# H60: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles in 1383 host cycles
# Without the option, the same staged registers (static-link-kinds.test BC).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bc0 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --share-links --compact-links --staged-links Lane 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BC0
# BC0: staged: 11 links, 232 register bits; compact
# BC0-NOT: staged memories
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/tree-arb
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/tz --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --compact-links --staged-links --staged-link-memories --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --class-at 'sl@*.slice' --class-at 'root@inner:arb' --class-at 'root@inner:*.join_arb' 'root+Bank' 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TREE
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/tz/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/tz/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/tz/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=60 | FileCheck %s
# TREE: staged: 11 links, 46 register bits; staged memories: 2 (4 links), 18 bits
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/staged-bits
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/sb --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --share-links --compact-links --staged-links --staged-link-memories Sw Lnk 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SB
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/sb/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/sb/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/sb/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/sb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+9 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/sb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+10 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# SB: staged: 13 links, 88 register bits; staged memories: 2 (8 links), 64 bits
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles
# With SLR groups (`--slr-groups`), a staged link (and its memory) within one group as without groups; one between
# groups is registered at its producer's group instead (never staged). Both exact.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/broadcast
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/sgs --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --share-links --compact-links --staged-links --staged-link-memories --slr-groups --slr-count 2 --slr-assign Lane:0,Top_model:0 Lane 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SGS
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/sgs/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/sgs/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/sgs/build.log 2>&1
